        "original_id": "9d0948a1-ffef-5f93-b87e-544ac0e39740",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alma Wade\n- Products: F.E.A.R., SAS: Secure Tomorrow, The Lost Mind of Dr. Brain\n- Companies: Monolith Productions, Sierra Entertainment, Sierra On-Line\n- Concepts: survival horror, first-person shooter, educational game series, Jupiter EX engine\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Monolith Productions introduced Alma Wade in F.E.A.R. as a major antagonist and key figure in the F.E.A.R. series.\n- Alma Wade is the central mystery at the core of the F.E.A.R. series.\n- F.E.A.R.: First Encounter Assault Recon is a survival horror first-person shooter video game developed by Monolith Productions and published by Sierra Entertainment.\n- SAS: Secure Tomorrow uses the Jupiter EX engine, which is similar or identical to the engine used in F.E.A.R..\n- The Lost Mind of Dr. Brain is the third installment in the educational Dr. Brain series and was created and published by Sierra On-Line.",
